Give the renderer what the Legend of Mana Remaster's HD art needs to be drawn,
and nothing more: two 2D array textures for the drawing shaders to sample (the
room pages at binding 1, the UI pictures at binding 2, with a sampler each),
calls to make, fill, mipmap and drop them, and a call that queues one quad in
the current batch with the page bits and layer it's given, so it draws in order
with everything else. Which pictures go where, what fits, how they're blended
and where cells are on a page are the port's (src/remaster/remaster_hd_art.c),
which calls these through its HD renderer provider. The drawing shaders come
from the port's src/gpu/shaders, with texture modes 3 and 4 for these.

